================================================================
REALTIONAL E8 LATTICE SPECIFICATION
================================================================

TYPE: RDG-SID Object
SID[E8] := ( S[E8], I[E8], D[E8] )

----------------------------------------------------------------
STRUCTURAL MODE (S)
S[E8] :=
{
  x ∈ ℤ^8  OR  x ∈ (ℤ + 1/2)^8
  such that  Σ_{i=1}^8 x_i ≡ 0 (mod 2)
}

This is the standard even-unimodular realization:
- integer D8 sublattice
- half-integer coset
- parity constraint on total coordinate sum

----------------------------------------------------------------
INTERACTION MODE (I)
I[E8](x, y) := Σ_{i=1}^8 x_i y_i

RDG-Q-mode norm:
Q[E8](x) := (1/2) I[E8](x, x)
Q[E8](x) ∈ ℤ  because E8 is even.

----------------------------------------------------------------
UNIMODULARITY CONDITION
Let {v_1, ..., v_8} be any ℤ-basis of S[E8].

Gram matrix:
G_{ij} := I[E8](v_i, v_j)

Unimodularity:
det(G) = 1

Equivalently:
S[E8] = S[E8]^∨  (self-dual lattice)

----------------------------------------------------------------
DYNAMICS MODE (D)
D[E8] := id

Meaning:
No coarse-graining, RG-flow, or deformation is imposed.
This is a declaration, not a consequence of evenness/unimodularity.

================================================================
RDG-THETA FUNCTIONAL
================================================================

Define:
q := exp( 2π i z )

Theta functional:
Θ[E8](z) := Σ_{x ∈ E8} exp( 2π i Q[E8](x) z )
          = Σ_{m ≥ 0} R[E8](m) q^m

RDG counting functional:
R[E8](m) := #{ x ∈ E8 : Q[E8](x) = m }

Since Q[E8](x) = (1/2) I[E8](x,x),
the squared norm is 2m.

================================================================
MODULAR ACTION (RDG-SID → PED COUPLING)
================================================================

T-transform:
M_T(z) := z + 1
Θ[E8](M_T(z)) = Θ[E8](z)

S-transform:
M_S(z) := -1 / z
Θ[E8](M_S(z)) = z^4 Θ[E8](z)

Reason:
rank(E8) = 8 ⇒ weight = 8/2 = 4

Thus:
Θ[E8](z) ∈ M_4(SL2(ℤ))

================================================================
PED-EISENSTEIN SERIES (WEIGHT 4)
================================================================

E4(z) := 1 + 240 Σ_{n ≥ 1} σ_3(n) q^n

Divisor function:
σ_3(n) := Σ_{d | n} d^3

Space of weight-4 modular forms:
M_4(SL2(ℤ)) = ℂ · E4

Normalization:
Both Θ[E8] and E4 have constant term 1.

Therefore:
Θ[E8](z) = E4(z)

================================================================
RDG COUNTING LAW FOR E8
================================================================

Since Θ[E8](z) = E4(z):

R[E8](n) = 240 σ_3(n)

Equivalently:
#{ x ∈ E8 : I[E8](x,x) = 2n } = 240 σ_3(n)

================================================================
RDG SUMMARY OF TYPES AND VARIABLES
================================================================

SID:
  S[E8]  = structural lattice set
  I[E8]  = relational metric pairing
  D[E8]  = declared dynamics (id)

PED:
  P_4(z) = E4(z)
  E      = σ_3(n)
  D_4    = holomorphic modular dynamics

Q-mode:
  Q[E8](x) = (1/2) I[E8](x,x)

Theta:
  Θ[E8](z) = Σ exp(2π i Q[E8](x) z)

Counting:
  R[E8](n) = 240 σ_3(n)

